Let's confirm the binding type

Run these commands:

strings.exe SumoGUI.exe | findstr /i "NetTcpBinding"

Then

strings.exe SumoGUI.exe | findstr /i "BasicHttpBinding"

Then

strings.exe SumoGUI.exe | findstr /i "WSHttpBinding"

Then

strings.exe SumoGUI.exe | findstr /i "CustomBinding"

These results will tell us exactly which WCF binding is used.

Next, search the config folder

Search for

*.config

especially

App.config
SumoGUI.exe.config
client.config

Open every config file.

Search for

system.serviceModel

or

binding

or

endpoint

This is where Microsoft stores WCF configuration.
